WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.372
While the King was fetching the Executioner, Alice heard the Queen shouting.

2
00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:11.393
"It sounds like the Queen is upset," Alice said to the Cheshire Cat.

3
00:00:11.394 --> 00:00:13.946
"She's yelling about the croquet game."

4
00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:18.667
The Cheshire Cat's head floated above Alice, but he didn't reply.

5
00:00:18.668 --> 00:00:23.193
She decided to find out what was going on.

6
00:00:23.194 --> 00:00:26.663
The croquet game was as strange as ever.

7
00:00:26.664 --> 00:00:31.990
"Off with his head!" the Queen shouted as Alice approached.

8
00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:37.983
The Queen pointed to another player. "Off with her head too!"

9
00:00:37.984 --> 00:00:42.131
"What did those players do?" Alice asked the White Rabbit.

10
00:00:42.132 --> 00:00:48.796
"They weren't paying attention, so they missed their turns," the White Rabbit replied.

11
00:00:48.797 --> 00:00:55.210
"Oh no!" Alice said. "I probably missed my turn when I was talking to the Cheshire Cat.

12
00:00:55.211 --> 00:01:03.914
I don't want to lose my head. I'd better hunt for my ball. I mean, my hedgehog."

13
00:01:03.915 --> 00:01:09.138
Alice quickly found her hedgehog, which was fighting with another hedgehog.

14
00:01:09.139 --> 00:01:12.542
She didn't try to separate them.

15
00:01:12.543 --> 00:01:16.509
"Where's my mallet? I mean, where's my flamingo?"

16
00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:20.794
She looked around and spotted her flamingo across the garden.

17
00:01:20.795 --> 00:01:26.541
By the time she grabbed it, the hedgehogs had stopped fighting.

18
00:01:26.542 --> 00:01:31.057
In fact, they were nowhere in sight.

19
00:01:31.058 --> 00:01:34.964
"It doesn't matter that they've disappeared," Alice said to herself.

20
00:01:34.965 --> 00:01:39.177
"There are no wickets anyway. All the soldiers have walked away."

21
00:01:39.178 --> 00:01:46.652
She tucked the flamingo under her arm and returned to the Cheshire Cat.

22
00:01:46.653 --> 00:01:51.021
She was surprised to find a crowd gathered below his head.

23
00:01:51.022 --> 00:01:54.289
There was a loud argument going on.

24
00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:58.480
The Executioner, the King, and the Queen were all talking at once.

25
00:01:58.481 --> 00:02:04.355
As soon as they spotted Alice, they turned to her and kept talking.

26
00:02:04.356 --> 00:02:12.679
"I can't understand you," Alice said. "Please take turns talking."

27
00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.150
The Executioner went first.

28
00:02:15.151 --> 00:02:18.801
"They want me to cut off this cat's head.

29
00:02:18.802 --> 00:02:22.265
But I can't cut off a head without a body.

30
00:02:22.266 --> 00:02:27.368
I've never done anything like that in my life."

31
00:02:27.369 --> 00:02:33.000
He crossed his arms. "And I'm not going to start now!"

32
00:02:33.001 --> 00:02:38.429
"Stop talking nonsense!" the King said.

33
00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:45.119
"All you need is the head, and you have a head here, which—"

34
00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.586
The Queen gave an impatient snort.

35
00:02:48.587 --> 00:02:56.872
"If somebody doesn't do something right now, I'll order everyone's head cut off!"

36
00:02:56.873 --> 00:03:01.844
After that threat everyone in the crowd looked frightened.

37
00:03:01.845 --> 00:03:05.625
Alice had a hard time thinking of anything to say.

38
00:03:05.626 --> 00:03:09.950
Finally she said, "The Cheshire Cat belongs to the Duchess.

39
00:03:09.951 --> 00:03:14.090
You'd better ask her what to do about it."

40
00:03:14.091 --> 00:03:19.262
"The Duchess is in prison," the Queen said to the Executioner.

41
00:03:19.263 --> 00:03:22.529
"Bring her here at once."

42
00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.980
The Executioner ran off to fetch the Duchess.

43
00:03:25.981 --> 00:03:31.013
The moment he was gone, the Cheshire Cat's head began to fade away.

44
00:03:31.014 --> 00:03:40.213
By the time the Executioner returned with the Duchess, the Cat had disappeared.

45
00:03:40.214 --> 00:03:51.212
While the King and the Executioner searched for the Cheshire Cat, everyone else played croquet.

46
00:03:51.213 --> 00:03:57.020
The Duchess tucked her arm into Alice's, and they walked away.

47
00:03:57.021 --> 00:04:03.579
"I'm so glad to see you again, my dear." The Duchess patted Alice's arm.

48
00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.080
"And I'm glad to see you," Alice replied.

49
00:04:07.081 --> 00:04:11.550
She was surprised that the Duchess was so friendly.

50
00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:14.629
Alice and the Duchess walked and talked.

51
00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:20.010
Alice wanted to ask about the Cheshire Cat, but the Duchess was busy talking.

52
00:04:20.011 --> 00:04:25.415
Suddenly the Duchess' voice died away, and her arm shook.

53
00:04:25.416 --> 00:04:30.602
Alice looked up and saw the Queen blocking their path.

54
00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:36.980
"A fine day, Your Majesty," the Duchess said in a weak voice.

55
00:04:36.981 --> 00:04:40.824
The Queen was not happy to see the Duchess.

56
00:04:40.825 --> 00:04:47.621
"Leave immediately or off with your head!" she shouted.

57
00:04:47.622 --> 00:04:53.226
The Duchess hurried away, and the Queen turned to Alice.

58
00:04:53.227 --> 00:05:01.698
"Let's join the game!"

